{
  "name": "lacewing",
  "_about": "A lacewing -- the common green lacewing (Chrysoperla carnea), 1 cm long with wings of 1.5 cm: delicate and pale green, with shining golden eyes and a pale stripe down its back; long thread antennae; four big clear wings, each a fine net of green veins, held steeply roof-like over the slender body and reaching far beyond it; thin pale legs. Coat: autumn (flushed brownish). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
